From 1e015021ef320c15c8806d78f1ecdbe25910438b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peet van de Sande <peet@peetvandesande.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:32:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add PROMETHEUS listener protocol

Octavia added the PROMETHEUS listener protocol in API version 2.25. It
exposes the load balancer's metrics in the Prometheus format, but the
dashboard did not offer it, so these listeners could only be created
from the CLI.

Offer PROMETHEUS in the listener protocol list. A PROMETHEUS listener
cannot have a default pool, so selecting it turns off pool and health
monitor creation in the wizard and locks those toggles, the pool is
removed from the request, and the default pool selection is hidden
when editing such a listener.

TLS on PROMETHEUS listeners is left for a follow-up.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
